WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.859 --> 00:00:06.040
Ruby Rose looks sensational in her Batwoman
costume, as the DC Comics superheroine prepares

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:07.960
to make the leap from page to screen.

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:12.460
The newest character in the CW's Arrowverse
hasn't quite touched down just yet, but the

00:00:12.469 --> 00:00:16.309
network has gone ahead and released a first
official look at how the character will appear

00:00:16.309 --> 00:00:18.860
when she makes her debut in an upcoming crossover
event.

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:22.780
To sum it up, she looks fierce, comics-accurate,
and perfectly-coiffed.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:24.300
The cape looks nice, too.

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:26.540
And all this just in time for Halloween.

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:30.620
Rose was cast as Batwoman in August, around
a month after reports first emerged that the

00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:33.740
CW was developing a live-action Batwoman series.

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:38.180
The new show will compliment the other DC
Comics superhero series on the network a lineup

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:42.410
which currently includes Arrow, The Flash,
Legends of Tomorrow, Supergirl, and Black

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:42.900
Lightning.

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:47.800
Unlike Black Lightning, which has so far largely
stood on its own in the CW's superhero slate,

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:51.440
Batwoman will associate itself with the other
heroes of the Arrowverse right from the jump.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:55.710
Prior to heading up her own series, the Batwoman
character will make her first appearance in

00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:59.780
the three-part Arrowverse crossover event
"Elseworlds", which is set to begin on Sunday,

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:01.860
December 9 with an episode of The Flash.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:06.080
The event will continue in an episode of Arrow
on Monday, December 10 and conclude with an

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:08.500
episode of Supergirl on Tuesday, December
11.

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:12.240
The Batwoman series proper will then follow
sometime in 2019.

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:16.800
While details on the story of the "Elseworlds"
crossover are somewhat scarce, the title alone

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:20.810
seems to imply that the Arrowverse will once
again be indulging in some alternate universe

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:25.420
shenanigans, as it has to great effect in
past crossover episodes like "Crisis On Earth-X".

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:29.820
DC has also announced that the team-up event
will introduce comics character The Monitor,

00:01:29.830 --> 00:01:34.900
a nearly-omnipotent, Multiverse-hopping entity
played by Designated Survivor's LaMonica Garrett.

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:38.740
The crossover will also feature first-ever
appearances from famed DC Comics reporter

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:43.470
Lois Lane, as well as the character Nora Fries,
better known as the wife of Mr. Freeze, whose

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:47.460
death notoriously drove the Gotham City villain
to a vengeful life of crime.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:51.820
Will the Flash, Arrow and Supergirl team up
to help Batwoman take on Mr. Freeze?

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:53.420
There's got to be more to it than that.

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:55.479
Mr. Freeze isn't that threatening.

00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:58.940
"Da blood will FREEEEEZE in ma hands!"

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:03.640
According to the CW, the crossover will follow
the established Arrowverse heroes (minus the

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:07.970
Legends of Tomorrow) as they travel to Gotham
City, presumably on some sort of crime-fighting

00:02:07.970 --> 00:02:08.520
adventure.

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:11.340
The question is, which Gotham City will they
be going to?

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:15.880
We know from Arrow and Supergirl that a Gotham
City exists on those two characters' Earths,

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:21.430
so will this be the Gotham of Earth-One, Earth-Thirty-Eight,
or another Earth we haven't visited before?

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:23.160
The opportunities are endless.

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:24.340
"How many are there?"

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:25.500
"Infinite."

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:29.580
The particular version of Batwoman that Rose
will be playing is Kate Kane, who has been

00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:33.209
presented in the comics as a wealthy heiress
in the Gotham City social scene.

00:02:33.209 --> 00:02:36.989
While we haven't seen her in action yet, reports
say that the character will be portrayed as

00:02:36.989 --> 00:02:41.010
an out-and-proud lesbian and capable street
fighter who is at first reluctant to don the

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:42.920
cape, the cowl, and the big red wig.

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:44.400
Aren't they always, though?

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:47.090
You can't take up a Bat-mantle without at
least a little inner turmoil.

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:48.800
"Do you want to talk about how you're feeling
right now?"

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:50.000
I don't talk about feelings.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:51.880
I don't have any, Alfred, I've never seen
one.

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:54.700
I'm a night stalking, crime fighting, vigilante."

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:58.200
It's hard to imagine how you could get much
closer to a live-action version of the comic

00:02:58.200 --> 00:02:59.220
book look than this.

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:03.740
Specifically, the design of the costume for
the TV series seems to be taking inspiration

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:07.260
from the version of the getup popularized
by the DC Comics series, 52.

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:11.480
The most distinguishing feature of the getup
is the voluminous shock of red hair cascading

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:15.640
out the back of the Batwoman cowl, which could
be mesmerizing to see in motion if it's done

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:16.140
well.

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:20.300
It's already a better red wig than the one
Marvel stuck poor Medusa with on that Inhumans

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:20.800
show.

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:24.960
The one thing this costume snapshot doesn't
address is where Batwoman intends to carry

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:25.720
all her stuff.

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:29.640
That's a pretty slim utility belt, after all;
Maybe the cape has pockets.

00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:34.040
Or maybe they're still planning on outfitting
Batwoman with her classic, 1950-era Bat-Purse

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:37.700
accessory, for those nights when she needs
to carry around a change of shoes along with

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:38.760
the baton and Batarangs.

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:42.240
These are the kinds of things you have to
think about when you're a fashion-forward

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:44.659
crime fighter Batman and Robin have it easy.

